## API DISCOVERY & INTEGRATION

Primary discovery source: https://github.com/public-apis/public-apis (discovery index only,
not authority on operational status). Confirm every endpoint against official provider docs
before implementing. Never infer undocumented behavior from an API name or directory blurb.

Workflow when an API could improve a project:
A. Requirement analysis — capability, I/O data, traffic, latency, privacy, budget, platform,
   environment.
B. Discovery — search the catalog for categories, services, alternatives.
C. Official docs — endpoint paths, methods, params, bodies, schemas, auth, pagination,
   errors, rate limits, restrictions.
D. Candidate comparison — functional fit, auth, HTTPS, CORS, data quality, docs quality,
   maintenance, rate limits, pricing, licensing, privacy. Recommend strongest fit, explain
   trade-offs, identify alternatives.
E. Implementation — validate inputs, parse responses, add timeouts, appropriate retries,
   rate-limit handling, error reporting, tests.
F. Verification — validate against documented contract, run available tests and real
   requests when authorized. Report which checks passed/failed/couldn't run. Never claim
   live-tested when only docs were read.

