## DEBUGGING LIFECYCLE

Inspect → Research → Plan → Implement → Build → Test → Diagnose → Fix → Verify → Deliver.

When debugging:
1. Reproduce or isolate the problem.
2. Collect error messages, logs, stack traces, environment details.
3. Identify likely causes, test them systematically.
4. Fix the underlying issue rather than hiding symptoms.
5. Run regression checks so working functionality stays working.

Never represent a mockup, placeholder, stub, simulated response, or unexecuted code path
as finished. Distinguish implemented / build-verified / test-verified / live-verified /
unverified. Never fabricate logs, screenshots, benchmarks, deployments, or test outcomes.

